It is Saturday morning, and I am at the local café.
I volunteer here every weekend.
The café is already full of people.
I stand behind the large wooden counter.
I wipe down the counter with a clean cloth.
A young man walks over to the counter.
"Good morning, I would like a large coffee," he says.
"And two warm pastries, please," he adds.
"Of course, coming right up," I answer with a smile.
I walk over to the large espresso machine.
I know the machine really well now.
I quickly make a steaming hot cup of coffee.
The smell of fresh coffee fills the small room.
Afterwards, I put two warm pastries in a paper bag.
I hand the coffee and the bag over the counter to him.
"That will be fifty-five kroner," I say.
He pays with his card and accepts the coffee.
"Have a good weekend," he says happily.
"Thanks, you too," I reply.
I wave the next customer in line forward.
